# profiling (new in 3.15): cProfile imports profiling.tracing at module load, so the
# package itself must stay. The sampling profiler's web-report assets (vendored d3 JS,
# logos, CSS/HTML templates, ~690KB that would survive .py deletion) are pure dead
# weight embedded; pruning them only degrades report generation, not `import profiling`.
profiling/sampling/_vendor
profiling/sampling/_assets
profiling/sampling/_flamegraph_assets
profiling/sampling/_heatmap_assets
profiling/sampling/_shared_assets
# Interactive-REPL / dev-only modules — never imported when running a script (embedded
# mode); plus easter eggs and frozen demo modules. _pyrepl is intentionally NOT pruned:
# CPython 3.14's pydoc and pdb import it at module load (3.15 made those imports
# guarded, but we keep it so pydoc / pdb / pytest keep full functionality).
rlcompleter*
tabnanny*
antigravity*
this*
__hello__*
__phello__
*/__pycache__